<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Free Officers Movement (Iraq)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1958">1958</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Free Officers were a secret network of Iraqi army officers, modelled on the Egyptian movement, led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abd-al-karim-qasim">Abd al-Karim Qasim</a> and Abdul Salam Arif. On 14 July 1958 their troops seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a>, killed King Faisal II and his family and proclaimed a republic. The revolution ended the Hashemite monarchy and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a>'s membership of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad-pact">Baghdad Pact</a>.</p></div>
